commit 32d51e5495254c0f762c9711d23dac1bba588617
Author: Daisuke Majima <rockyshikoku@gmail.com>
Date:   Wed May 27 05:04:24 2026 +0900

    Share the fused gated-delta kernel between MLXLLM and MLXVLM
    
    Move `GatedDelta.swift` to `MLXLMCommon`; fix VLM kernel dispatch
    
    `GatedDelta.swift` defines a fused Metal kernel (`gatedDeltaKernel`, single threadgroup over the time loop) and an `gatedDeltaOps` fallback. `gatedDeltaUpdate` prefers the kernel when MLX Metal is available — the only path taken by Qwen 3.5 / Qwen 3 Next on Apple Silicon.
    
    `MLXVLM/Models/Qwen35.swift` was a copy of the same file with the kernel branch omitted, so every VLM Qwen 3.5 checkpoint using `linear_attn` fell through to the unfused per-step expression-graph path, producing far more intermediates per token.
    
    - Move `GatedDelta.swift` to `MLXLMCommon`, mark `gatedDeltaUpdate` public (helpers stay internal)
    - Remove the duplicate from `MLXVLM/Models/Qwen35.swift` so the VLM call site shares the same kernel-preferred dispatch as the LLM side
    - Update `Tests/MLXLMTests/GatedDeltaTests.swift` to import `MLXLMCommon` instead of `@testable import MLXLLM`
    
    No behavior change for MLXLLM. MLXVLM Qwen 3.5 with `linear_attn` now uses the fused kernel.

